course: dictionary
lesson: 4974
title: Words that will not change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a person or animal whose habits will not change, however often people try to help. The word is incorrigible. In- often means "not", and corrigible means "able to be corrected", so incorrigible means cannot be put right.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad's friends try again and again to cure him of his craze for motor cars, but he goes straight back to it. The Chairman calls him «the incorrigible rogue and hardened ruffian». A rogue is a dishonest character, so the Chairman means Toad is bad and cannot be made better.
explain: Used playfully, incorrigible means always up to something naughty or silly, in a way people half like. If someone says, «You're incorrigible!» with a smile, they are teasing you, not telling you off. Look at the face and tone to tell which meaning is meant.
fact: Incorrigible means cannot be corrected or made better.
fact: In- often means "not", as in unhappy, so incorrigible points to something that cannot be fixed.
fact: «Incorrigible» can describe a bad habit, a naughty pet or a cheeky character.
fact: When it is said playfully, with a smile, it means someone is always being naughty or silly.
fact: The opposite of incorrigible is correctable, meaning able to be put right.
exercise: «The Chairman called Toad an incorrigible rogue.» What does incorrigible mean here? | *Cannot be made better | Hungry for food | Very rich and famous | Frightened of the judge
exercise: Mum laughs and says, «You're incorrigible!» What does she mean? | Go to bed now | You have won the prize | *You are always being naughty or silly, and she half likes it | You are very ill and need a doctor
exercise: Toad's friends try again and again to cure him, but he goes back to his craze every time. What clue shows that he is incorrigible? | *He goes back to his craze every time | His friends try to help him | Toad is fond of motor cars | Toad lives by the river
test: «My puppy is incorrigible: he chews my shoes every single day, even after many telling-offs.» What does incorrigible suggest? | He is very clever at maths | *He will not stop his bad habit | He is tired and wants to sleep | He has just learned a new trick
test: Which word means the opposite of incorrigible? | *Correctable | Naughty | Cheeky | Silly
exam: Jayden says his big sister is incorrigible, and she laughs and smiles back at him. Which is the best explanation? | *He is teasing her playfully, meaning she is always up to something silly | He means she has been corrected and is now perfect | Her habits are dangerous and she needs a doctor | He means she is asleep and cannot be woken
